 (report . "Ten independent review rounds against the frozen W6 wave doc, ending with R10 APPROVED at this exact head. R1 refused three vacuities: F3/F12 shared an incomplete trio fixture, the clean controls did not require exit 0 plus the pass line, and neither the rehearsal inputs nor the suite witness were bound (no inputs digest, no minimum test count, no assertion evidence). R2 refused rows whose only observation was a token while the guard exited non-zero, and an F12 row still labelled library. R3 caught that the R2 F12 patch had been applied without its assertions (a silent no-op). R4 refused vacuous clean controls for F7/F8/F9 (accepting anything that did not crash instead of the typed success observation). R5 refused the F4 clean control matching 'pure' inside 'impure-record-commit' and F2/suite witnesses ignoring exit codes. R6 refused token witnesses accepting a non-zero tool failure as a decided verdict and suite witnesses satisfied by tokens in comments. R7 refused tokens sitting in a comment inside an asserting block (now assertion windows) and a pinned rehearsal head that could lag the reviewed tip (now the generation-time tip). R8 refused the two suite guards not being rehearsal inputs (a vacuous passing suite could leave the matrix byte-identical) and stale report head text. R9 refused a guard exiting 0 while printing both the refusal and the success verdict (now verdict-LINE semantics with contradictory-verdict rejection) and report/matrix head drift (now generator-synced and test-asserted). Every refused round was falsified end to end before or after the fix with a concrete scratch-tree repro; the retained falsifications are recorded in the report. R10 verified the remediations and found no remaining defect that breaks the frozen W6 guarantee. APPROVED."))